Z||000006||Gold-86SE||05-28-2000||11:01 PM||||<BR>Dan, sorry it took so long to make the post, been out-of-pocket since friday evening. btw, i did not make it to waco, but if the t-storm line that hit waco resembled anything like the one in austin, i am glad i missed it. I would have had to drive i-35 from waco to s.a. in rain. blah....<P>I work for insurance rating systems in universal city <A HREF="http://www.irsaims.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.irsaims.com</A> <P>been there going on 3 years, has been interesting, not so much fun. but padding for my resume.<P>as for the lizano brothers, i hesitate to admit my ignorance but i do not know who they are. but if they can put a blown 426 hemi in my 86 that would be a rush.<P>Additionally, i have been thinking about starting a fiero ride once a quarter here in the south texas area.  Just getting together with a few fellow owners who are relatively close, so that we could take a saturday afternoon/evening drive thru some of the texas countryside.  I have not worked out all the details, but the following is my concern.<P>I am a member of the alamo area fiero owners club and the club sponsors the april fiero roundup once a year. this year was my first roundup and it was extremely fun and i was told that the club participates in other car shows.<P>i don't want to irritate the club, but getting together once a year for the big fiero roundup and participating in some of the car shows is not the same thing as meeting with a few fellow fiero owners and taking a hill country ride for 2-3 hours.<P>If such a saturday afternoon/evening event was available 3/4 times a year, would you participate? And/or do you know of others who would want to participate?<P>I really think it is a cool idea, but I don't want to ruffle feathers with the club.<BR>||||reg||1
